# ── Native runtime binaries ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provisioned by `synheart install runtime`; never committed. The vendored
# tree under example/ is ~1.8 GB, so an unguarded `git add .` is expensive.
# Mirrors the ignore rules in the Flutter SDK.

# Native shared libraries (loaded at runtime, not committed)
*.so
*.dylib

# Host-side test runtime — synheart-core/build.gradle points
# `jna.library.path` here.
native/

# Everything `synheart install runtime` drops into the example app — vendored
# native runtimes, xcframeworks and the syni spec bundle. Machine-specific,
# large, and re-fetched by the CLI, so the whole tree stays out rather than just
# `vendor/`: a future CLI layout change should not start committing binaries.
example/synheart/

# ── Example app credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Downloaded from platform.synheart.ai. The four ids are identifiers rather
# than secrets, but they are organization-specific, so a populated file stays
# local. Only the placeholder template is checked in — README and SETUP tell you
# to copy it, so a fresh clone needs it present. Mirrors the Flutter SDK.
# `example/env/*` and not `example/env/`: git never descends into an ignored
# DIRECTORY, so a negation for a file inside one has no effect and the template
# below would be ignored too.
example/env/*
!example/env/synheart.credentials.example.json

# Agent instruction files. Local working guidance, not part of the published
# SDK — kept out of the repo so it can be edited freely without a review cycle.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
